## Boundary rules

- This file carries cross-project facts only; member-internal details are always linked to the member's `AGENTS.md` or `aiDoc/README.md`, never copied.
- Conflict priority: a member's own `AGENTS.md` governs its internal affairs; this file governs cross-project coordination.
- When a member project is added or removed, update the member index table in the same change.
- Decision records, evidence discipline, handoffs and other operating invariants follow each member repo's own conventions; a cross-project change leaves a trail in every affected member repo under its own process.
